   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Ember Burn\n\nThe outgoing frame is set on fire: a noisy burn front eats the bright parts first, the edge boils and glows, charred rims fall away and sparks drift off carrying the frame's colour, uncovering the next scene. Runs its WebGL shader over two built-in panels (a stat and a bar chart, then a render queue; text and colours from variables), not over the host's scenes: 60 frames of the first panel, a 40-frame transition, then the second panel. To use it between your own scenes, copy the shader into your composition and feed it your two frames as textures.\n\nCategory: transitions. Length: 5.3333 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- A scene change should feel cinematic and physical: the frame is destroyed rather than blended away.\n- The moment can afford well over a second; the burn is meant to be watched.\n- The outgoing scene has real content worth consuming: the fire takes the bright parts first.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The cut has to be quick: a burn compressed under 24 frames reads as a smear; use zoom-blur.\n- The scenes are cool-toned or clinical and a warm flare would fight the palette: use grain-dissolve.\n\nVariables:\n- label (string): Label, default \"Deploys this week\"\n- value (string): Value, default \"2,481\"\n- bars (string): Bars, default \"32,51,43,68,57,86,64,100\"\n- accent (color): Highlight, default \"#a1eebd\"\n- title (string): Title, default \"Render queue\"\n- items (string): Rows, default \"intro-scene.mp4 | Done; feature-tour.mp4 | Rendering; pricing-outro.mp4 | Queued\"\n- background (color): Background, default \"#101828\"\n- patches (number, 2-16): Patches, default 5\n- edge_softness (number, 0.005-0.2): Edge softness, default 0.07\n- content_bias (number, 0-1): Content bias, default 0.6\n- heat (number, 0-1.5): Heat, default 0.5\n- glow_color (color): Glow, default \"#ff7a2f\"\n- ember_amount (number, 0-1): Embers, default 0.5\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.75\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
